From ff75f2db1de0f0f0d6d0aa1facb640d4b4630fb8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "D. Zack Garza" <dzackgarza@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 01:32:43 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 14/16] fix: deploy the repair as an ordered list of checked
 patches

A second patch corrects the Meson fallback chain, and a copy already carrying
the first must not have its recorded provenance overwritten by new bytes under
the same name. apply-bliss-repair.sh now takes the patches in order, applies only
the ones a copy does not already carry, explains every locally modified file by
a patch it already carries, and records each patch's digest in the stamp
alongside the module digest. A rebuild happens only when a patch was applied or
the installed module is not the one the stamp records; a failure reverts the
patches that run applied.

Verified on the published unpacked copy: the first patch was recognised as
already present and skipped, the correction applied, the module rebuilt and
installed (4518 unchanged files), the smoke tests passed, and the stamp now
lists both digests -- baf4b826... for the original repair and ff86f4a9... for the
correction -- with the same module digest as before, since the correction
changes only which library the configure accepts, not the code compiled here.

SAGE-ENVIRONMENT.md says the same, and that a copy carrying the first patch
alone is correct for this image but is not evidence that the fallback works.
